From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800_fdrv: bound the AP entry to sta_flowctrl[] in
 sm_connect_ind

rwnx_rx_sm_connect_ind() reads sta_flowctrl[sta->sta_idx] for the AP
entry. ap_idx comes from the device and is checked against sta_table[]
(NX_REMOTE_STA_MAX + NX_VIRT_DEV_MAX entries), but sta_flowctrl[] has
only NX_REMOTE_STA_MAX entries, so an AP index in the last
NX_VIRT_DEV_MAX slots reads past it.

Read the pending count only for an index below NX_REMOTE_STA_MAX.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
index cf1c0d7..036353d 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_msg_rx.c
@@ -998,7 +998,9 @@ static inline int rwnx_rx_sm_connect_ind(struct rwnx_hw *rwnx_hw,
             rwnx_vif->tdls_chsw_prohibited = extcap->ext_capab[4] & WLAN_EXT_CAPA5_TDLS_CH_SW_PROHIBITED;
         }
 
-		if(atomic_read(&rwnx_hw->sta_flowctrl[sta->sta_idx].tx_pending_cnt) > 0) {
+		/* sta_flowctrl[] has only NX_REMOTE_STA_MAX entries */
+		if(sta->sta_idx < NX_REMOTE_STA_MAX &&
+		   atomic_read(&rwnx_hw->sta_flowctrl[sta->sta_idx].tx_pending_cnt) > 0) {
 			AICWFDBG(LOGDEBUG, "sta idx %d fc error %d\n",  sta->sta_idx,  atomic_read(&rwnx_hw->sta_flowctrl[sta->sta_idx].tx_pending_cnt));
 		}
 
